WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.410
Hi there, Steve Kaufman here again,
and I want to talk again about

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:08.100
ChatGPT, artificial intelligence
and its impact on language learning.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.040
You know, I enjoy doing these videos.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.610
Uh, some people say, you know,
you always say the same thing,

00:00:14.615 --> 00:00:15.930
you're a big bag of wind, whatever.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.450
I don't mind, people are
entitled to their opinions.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.380
Uh, but I do enjoy doing these
videos and sharing my ideas

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.849
with you, and I get feedback.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.445
One person said, you know, the effect
of GPT is going to, to render all the

00:00:29.855 --> 00:00:32.295
language learning apps, uh, irrelevant.

00:00:33.015 --> 00:00:37.724
Uh, there's also fear on the part
of some that it'll, uh, you know,

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:39.315
affect the role of the teacher.

00:00:41.025 --> 00:00:43.215
I don't think it should.

00:00:43.905 --> 00:00:45.735
Uh, and I'm gonna explain why.

00:00:45.825 --> 00:00:51.045
So, if I look at Duolingo, which
has, uh, apparently incorporated some

00:00:51.045 --> 00:00:56.489
aspects of ChatGPT in their system,
I don't fully know how, and, and, and

00:00:56.489 --> 00:01:00.989
all the details, but I, I looked it up
on the, on, you know, Google and what

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:06.000
they're incorporating is essentially
role playing and error correction.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:13.860
So yeah, it's possible that, um, a
person could sort of individually set

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.539
up role playing activities with ChatGPT.

00:01:18.134 --> 00:01:23.856
Uh, and in these role playing activities,
ChatGPT could also correct whatever it

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:31.124
is that they type in to their, you know,
dialogue with ChatGPT, uh, independently.

00:01:31.214 --> 00:01:35.684
Uh, a learner could, could
write an essay or whatever and

00:01:35.684 --> 00:01:38.395
have it corrected by ChatGPT.

00:01:39.195 --> 00:01:41.505
So does that make the teacher unnecessary?

00:01:42.164 --> 00:01:42.795
I don't think so.

00:01:42.795 --> 00:01:44.115
I think we have to look at...

00:01:44.265 --> 00:01:49.095
and, and by the way, I saw on some of the
websites that I visited, the suggestion

00:01:49.095 --> 00:01:55.755
that well, uh, you know, ChatGPT may
lighten the load for teachers or might

00:01:55.755 --> 00:02:02.235
make it, you know, less necessary to go
to, uh, you know, uh, substitute teachers.

00:02:02.595 --> 00:02:07.545
This idea that there's this hierarchy
of established teachers, permanent

00:02:07.545 --> 00:02:11.340
teachers, and substitute teachers,
I don't see a big difference between

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:16.710
them, because basically the role of
the teacher is to motivate the learner.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.860
The classroom is largely a social place.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.490
It's where people meet, it's where
the students meet each other.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.320
It's where the teacher meets the students.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.390
In an ideal scenario, out of this
classroom environment comes an

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.990
enthusiasm for learning the language.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.010
That's what happened to me, not the 10
years that I did French school, where

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:43.800
the classroom was just boring, but when
in first year university at McGill,

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:48.600
I had a professor that made French
civilization so fascinating for me

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.510
that I decided to really pursue French.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:57.540
So that's an example of the vital
role that a teacher can play, and it's

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:04.740
possible with ChatGPT because ChatGPT
can generate, uh, content, can correct

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:13.245
things, provide a motivated learner with
some opportunity for, you know, studying

00:03:13.245 --> 00:03:18.495
on his or her own, having his or her
material corrected, or maybe before

00:03:18.495 --> 00:03:20.805
submitting an essay, having it corrected.

00:03:20.985 --> 00:03:25.365
Or in the worst case, having
ChatGPTwrite the essay for him or

00:03:25.365 --> 00:03:29.685
her, which I gather they're looking
at ways of, you know, making that more

00:03:29.685 --> 00:03:31.365
difficult to do without being detected.

00:03:32.535 --> 00:03:37.905
So some of these opportunities are there,
but the teacher, whether substitute

00:03:37.905 --> 00:03:43.995
or the main tenured teacher, call it,
still has this tremendously important

00:03:43.995 --> 00:03:46.395
social role because language is social.

00:03:47.135 --> 00:03:48.135
Language is communicating.

00:03:48.555 --> 00:03:52.515
Communicating with people, communicating
with history, communicating with

00:03:52.515 --> 00:03:57.195
sound, communicating with the written
word, and it's up to the teacher to

00:03:57.195 --> 00:04:00.405
make that motivating, interesting.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:08.580
And, and certainly as an independent
learner, I would not use ChatGPT

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.340
for correcting my writing.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.690
I have no interest in that.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:17.070
Um, my use of the language
will be what it is.

00:04:17.075 --> 00:04:22.200
It'll gradually improve as I talk
to people, as I hear how the native

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:26.310
speaker uses the language, as I listen
to content of interest I expect that

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:31.470
my vocabulary will grow, my familiarity
with the language will, uh, increase

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:36.660
and, uh, the frequency of my areas
will gradually, you know, diminish.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.850
Um, but I know from experience
that being corrected doesn't mean

00:04:41.855 --> 00:04:43.170
that I get it right the next time.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:45.930
So it's just, you know, yeah, if...

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:49.920
I'll do what I feel like doing in the
language and that probably will not

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.685
include an essay for ChatGPT to correct.

00:04:54.135 --> 00:04:58.255
I am personally also not interested
in having a role playing exercise

00:04:58.785 --> 00:05:04.455
with a ChatGPT, however, I can see
where a teacher could assign that.

00:05:05.145 --> 00:05:11.775
Uh, and therefore the ChatGPT then is
a resource available to the teacher to,

00:05:11.835 --> 00:05:18.075
you know, assign an activity, say role
playing or interacting with ChatGPT.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:24.000
Or, uh, asking a student to write
something for ChatGPT to correct,

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:27.750
which therefore means that the
teacher doesn't have to correct it.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:32.490
So there are all these ways
in which ChatGPT becomes, uh,

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.860
uh, an assist to the teacher.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:39.900
Even though it's not a great interest
to an independent learner like me, it

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:45.360
enables the teacher to, uh, you know,
achieve what the curriculum requires

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.815
the teacher to do in the classroom.

00:05:47.135 --> 00:05:50.925
But fundamentally, the
teacher to me is a mo...

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:57.195
a motivator, and I don't think ChatGPT
is gonna remove or substitute for

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:02.565
the need for a teacher to motivate
learners, but it can be used by a

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:08.205
teacher to lighten their load in terms
of correction, in terms of dreaming up

00:06:08.265 --> 00:06:14.535
role playing situations, uh, and for the
truly independent learner like myself,

00:06:15.215 --> 00:06:18.975
probably not all that relevant in those
roles, in the roles that dual lingo has

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:22.195
decided to, you know, assign to cChatGPT.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:27.615
However, where I am more optimistic
is, is using ChatGPT to help

00:06:27.615 --> 00:06:32.760
generate, you know, learner content
at, particularly at the intermediate

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.890
or beginner, intermediate level.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:42.180
Uh, but even then, as I've said before,
we need to consume so much content and

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:47.010
ultimately we want to have compelling,
interesting content, authentic content.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:51.150
And so ChatGPT would have a limited role.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:56.010
Uh, I am much more interested in seeing
how we can use Whisper or some of this

00:06:56.010 --> 00:07:02.460
other technology to facilitate the
transcription of the massive amount of

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:07.650
excellent compelling audio content that
exists and how we can better integrate

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:13.410
that into a, you know, uh, a learning
platform light LingQ with our sentence

00:07:13.415 --> 00:07:15.360
view, maybe better timestamping.

00:07:15.765 --> 00:07:19.875
These kinds of things to facilitate
or to make it more efficient and

00:07:19.875 --> 00:07:23.835
more compelling for learners and
make it easier for learners to access

00:07:23.835 --> 00:07:28.115
more difficult content using the
functionality that we have at LingQ.

00:07:28.425 --> 00:07:33.915
So those are the kinds of applications
that I see for AI call it, or maybe, uh,

00:07:33.915 --> 00:07:38.325
improved, uh, text to speech where we
don't notice the difference between the,

00:07:38.325 --> 00:07:40.695
uh, natural voice and text to speech.

00:07:40.695 --> 00:07:42.435
Those are some of the things
that I'm more hopeful.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:47.310
Uh, to me at least as an independent
learner, I think ChatGPT has

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:48.690
more limited application.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:53.760
However, I can see where it can, uh,
lessen the burden of language teachers.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:58.360
So a little bit of a, you know, a
meandering piece there on ChatGPT

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:03.240
again, and, and, and whether it
will actually threaten, uh, language

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:07.275
learning apps as one of my viewers
suggested, like LingQ for example,

00:08:07.545 --> 00:08:09.225
or threaten the role of teachers.

00:08:09.285 --> 00:08:12.765
So I hope you found, you found that
interesting and uh, you can have a

00:08:12.765 --> 00:08:15.315
look at some of the other discussions
on this subject that I've had.

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:16.215
Bye for now.

